• T4 is done. `npm run build` exits 0 with zero TypeScript errors under strict mode.

  **What was built** — all in `frontend/src/components/charts/`, hand-built SVG, no library added (scale maths turned out to be a 20-line `niceTicks`, so I skipped d3-scale entirely):

  - `LinePlot.tsx` — shared line engine (grid, crosshair + tooltip, keyboard cursor, legend, direct labels) behind the two line charts
  - `Sparkline.tsx` — replaces the history list in `DeviceDrawer`; single series in `var(--series-1)`, title names the metric
  - `UptimeTimeline.tsx` — one row per site, 48 half-hour buckets, rounded segments with 2px surface gaps, arrow-key cursor
  - `StatusDistribution.tsx` — stacked bar, worst-first, reserved status tokens with the icon+label `StatusBadge` legend
  - `MetricLine.tsx` — fleet health **per kind** (% reporting good), because the timeline already slices by site; camera→series-1 … thermostat→series-4 fixed map, intercoms fold into "Other" in muted grey
  - `ChartSection.tsx` — replaces the DashboardPage placeholder, receives the filtered fleet so charts compose with filters

  **Three defects found by looking at screenshots and fixed:**

  1. Historical buckets read as offline everywhere — the 5-min backfill grid is coarser than reporting intervals, so `statusAt` now floors staleness at the history resolution.
  2. The timeline was a wall of red: worst-of-1-device pins 5 of 6 sites at critical for all 48 buckets (verified numerically against the seeded fleet). Semantics are now "worst status shared by ≥2 devices" — single-device faults already show in the Pulse/grid/drawer; site rows now show episodes, flicker and recovery.
  3. X-axis tick collisions at drawer width — tick count now follows plot width (2–5 ticks), 24h `HH:MM` format.

  **Verified via headless Chrome + CDP:** 1440px and 360px screenshots (no collisions or overflow), hover tooltips on line charts and segments, Chart/Table toggles, drawer open flow, and the rule-2 case — filtering to Kind=fridge leaves the line wearing `var(--series-3)` with a "Fridges · 92 %" direct label. Console: zero errors.

